WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
SPEAKER: In this
Cloud Minute, you'll

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.410
learn how to quickly
deploy a Spring Boot

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.830
application to Google App
Engine standard for Java 11

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.820
using a JAR file.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.340
First, create a Spring
Boot application

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.980
from Spring Initializer.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.910
Add the Web Starter so you
can respond to web requests.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.910
In the Generate the Application,
create a controller that simply

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.030
returns hello from App Engine.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.280
Boot the application and
the package the JAR file.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.020
Use gcloud command
to deploy the JAR.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.720
Once deployed, you can
access the application

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.950
with the projects
URL on appspot.com.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.760
Alternatively, you can also
create an app.yaml file

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.550
to configure instance class,
environmental variable,

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.530
and deploy this
application directly

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:52.510
with Maven or Gradle
using App Engine plugins.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.820
Learn more about App
Engine standard Java 11

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.240
runtime on the
documentation website.

